body:
`EMPTY_TABLE_CELL` is a single object instance that gets inserted into the document multiple times. In Slate this risks multiple cells sharing the same node object reference, so editing one cell could unintentionally affect others and/or break normalization. Prefer a factory function (or deep clone) to create a fresh table-cell node each time you insert one.
```suggestion
function createEmptyTableCell(): TableCellNode {
  return {
    type: 'table-cell',
    children: [
      {
        type: 'paragraph',
        children: [{ text: '' }],
      },
    ],
  };
}
```

