body:
The `Dispose` method has a potential concurrency issue. When iterating over `_allocatedItems` and calling `Dispose()` on each item, the items themselves call `UntrackItem()` which modifies the `_allocatedItems` collection during iteration. While `ConcurrentDictionary` allows concurrent modifications, iterating with `foreach` over a collection being modified can lead to unpredictable behavior.

Additionally, this method lacks an idempotent dispose pattern - it should track whether it has already been disposed and return early on subsequent calls.

**Suggested fix:**
```csharp
private bool _disposed;

public void Dispose()
{
    if (_disposed)
    {
        return;
    }

    _disposed = true;

    if (_preserveTempFiles)
    {
        _logger?.LogInformation("Skipping cleanup of {Count} temporary files/directories due to ASPIRE_PRESERVE_TEMP_FILES configuration", _allocatedItems.Count);
        return;
    }

    if (_allocatedItems.IsEmpty)
    {
        return;
    }

    _logger?.LogDebug("Cleaning up {Count} remaining temporary files/directories", _allocatedItems.Count);

    // Take a snapshot to avoid modification during iteration
    var itemsToDispose = _allocatedItems.Values.ToList();
    foreach (var item in itemsToDispose)
    {
        try
        {
            item.Dispose();
        }
        catch (Exception ex)
        {
            _logger?.LogWarning(ex, "Failed to clean up temporary item");
        }
    }
}
```

