body:
The path traversal check has a logic error. On Windows, `path.sep` could be `\`, but this check would fail for paths at the repo root. The condition `fullPath !== repoRoot` is insufficient because it only checks exact equality. 

Consider using:
```javascript
if (!fullPath.startsWith(repoRoot + path.sep) && fullPath !== repoRoot) {
```

However, a more robust check would be:
```javascript
const normalizedFull = path.normalize(fullPath);
const normalizedRoot = path.normalize(repoRoot);
if (!normalizedFull.startsWith(normalizedRoot + path.sep) && normalizedFull !== normalizedRoot) {
  return `[Access denied: ${filePath} is outside the repository]`;
}
```

This ensures proper comparison even with trailing separators or path normalization issues.
```suggestion
      const normalizedFull = path.normalize(fullPath);
      const normalizedRoot = path.normalize(repoRoot);
      if (!normalizedFull.startsWith(normalizedRoot + path.sep) && normalizedFull !== normalizedRoot) {
```

