body:
The validation checks for `name` and `executable` are redundant. `ArgumentException.ThrowIfNullOrWhiteSpace` (lines 62, 64) already performs a null check, making the `ArgumentNullException.ThrowIfNull` calls (lines 61, 63) unnecessary.

Consider removing the explicit null checks:
```csharp
ArgumentException.ThrowIfNullOrWhiteSpace(name);
ArgumentException.ThrowIfNullOrWhiteSpace(executable);
```

This reduces code duplication and follows the DRY principle.
```suggestion
        ArgumentException.ThrowIfNullOrWhiteSpace(name);
```

