body:
The documentation states that "CommonJS `require`s are not detected for ignored packages" which is accurate, but this conflicts with the original issue comments which suggested that CommonJS require statements should also pass (e.g., `const { EventEmitter } = require("@angular/core")`). The PR description's "What works" section doesn't mention CommonJS at all, though one of the original test cases included it. Consider clarifying in the documentation why CommonJS is not supported or add support for it to match the upstream ESLint behavior more completely.
```suggestion
    /// Note that only ES module `import` statements are analyzed when
    /// determining whether `EventEmitter` comes from an ignored package.
    /// CommonJS `require` calls (for example,
    /// `const { EventEmitter } = require("@angular/core")`) are not
    /// currently detected for this exemption, so they will still be
    /// reported by this rule. Use ES6-style imports instead if you need
    /// `EventEmitter` from an ignored package to be allowed.
```

